.Dd July 27, 2026
.Dt SECUREDKIM-GENKEY 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm securedkim-genkey
.Nd generate DKIM keypair and DNS record
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl s Ar selector
.Fl d Ar domain
.Fl o Ar keyfile
.Op Fl a Ar algorithm
.Op Fl b Ar bits
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
generates a DKIM private key and prints the corresponding DNS TXT record
to standard output.
The private key is written to the specified output file.
.Pp
The generated DNS TXT record is ready to be added to the domain's DNS zone
at
.Ar selector Ns ._domainkey. Ns Ar domain .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl s Ar selector
DKIM selector name.
Required.
This becomes part of the DNS lookup key.
.It Fl d Ar domain
Domain name the key is generated for.
Required.
.It Fl o Ar keyfile
Output path for the private key file.
Required.
The file is created with mode 0600.
.It Fl a Ar algorithm
Key algorithm:
.Dq rsa
(default) or
.Dq ed25519 .
.It Fl b Ar bits
RSA key size in bits: 2048 (default) or 4096.
Ignored for Ed25519.
.It Fl h
Display usage information.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Generate a 2048-bit RSA key:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
securedkim-genkey -s 2026 -d example.com -o /usr/local/etc/securedkim/example.key
.Ed
.Pp
Generate an Ed25519 key:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
securedkim-genkey -a ed25519 -s ed2026 -d example.com -o /usr/local/etc/securedkim/example-ed.key
.Ed
.Pp
Generate a 4096-bit RSA key:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
securedkim-genkey -b 4096 -s strong2026 -d example.com -o /path/to/key.pem
.Ed
.Sh OUTPUT
The DNS TXT record is printed to stdout in a format suitable for direct
inclusion in a zone file:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
selector._domainkey.example.com. IN TXT "v=DKIM1; k=rsa; p=MIIBIj..."
.Ed
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr securedkim 8 ,
.Xr securedkim-testkey 8
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
.%T DomainKeys Identified Mail (DKIM) Signatures
.%R RFC 6376
.Re
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Daniel Morante
